package Physics.Tests

use Libraries.Game.Collision.LocalCollisionPoints3D
use Libraries.Game.Collision.Shapes.Triangle

/*
A triangle standing on end below the box, with its top corner just under
the box's bottom face. The triangle's normal points sideways and overlaps
a lot, so the box's up axis is the best direction, and the one contact is
the triangle's top corner, moved onto the box face. With the margin, the
corner reaches 0.05 into the box.

Unless a test says otherwise, the triangle is a large one lying flat
at height 0, from MakeLargeTriangle, with the usual margin of 0.04, so
its thickened surface is at 0.04. The box is 0.5 on each side for
collisions (see RunBox), with no rotation, and the triangle is item A.
A box whose center is at 0.28 has its bottom at 0.03, so it sinks 0.01
into the surface.
*/
class BoxTriangleFaceDirectionTest is PhysicsTest
    on create
        SetName("Box and triangle: box face direction")
    end

    action Run
        Triangle triangle
        triangle:Set(MakeVector(0.1, -0.24, 0), MakeVector(0.1, -0.6, 0.3), MakeVector(0.1, -0.6, -0.3))
        triangle:SetMargin(0.04)
        LocalCollisionPoints3D points = RunBox(triangle, MakeTransform(0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0), false)
        CheckContact("box face direction", points, 0, -1, 0, 0.1, -0.25, 0, -0.05)
    end
end
